	<title>Steppenwolf</title>
	<isbn>0140282580</isbn>
	<publication_year>1999</publication_year>
	<language_code>eng</language_code>
	<description>&lt;i&gt;Steppenwolf&lt;/i&gt; is a poetical self-portrait of a man who felt himself to be half-human and half-wolf. This Faust-like and magical story is evidence of Hesse's searching philosophy and extraordinary sense of humanity as he tells of the humanization of a middle-aged misanthrope. Yet this novel can also be seen as a plea for rigorous self-examination and an indictment of the intellectual hypocrisy of the period. As Hesse himself remarked, "Of all my books &lt;i&gt;Steppenwolf&lt;/i&gt; is the one that was more often and more violently misunderstood than any other".</description>
